From 623b70d430e7e659fd8e9bbb6460281a59a46215 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Fairfield <tom@fairfieldt.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 22:18:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] PCI/P2PDMA: Add Intel Xeon E5 v2 (Ivy Bridge-EP) to allowlist

The allowlist has the Sandy Bridge-EP (0x3c00), Haswell-EP (0x2f00) and
Broadwell-EP (0x6f00) host bridges but not Ivy Bridge-EP, the generation
between Sandy Bridge-EP and Haswell-EP, so peer-to-peer DMA between
devices on its root ports is refused.

Add the Xeon E7 v2/Xeon E5 v2/Core i7 DMI2 host bridge (0x0e00) with
REQ_SAME_HOST_BRIDGE, like its neighbours.

Tested on a Mac Pro 6,1 (Xeon E5-2697 v2), whose two FirePro D700 GPUs
sit on root ports 00:02.0 and 00:03.0 of that host bridge, with the
Intel IOMMU enabled in translated mode.  Each GPU in turn imported the
other's VRAM as a dma-buf, so amdgpu mapped the peer BAR with
dma_map_resource() and the buffer stayed in VRAM instead of migrating to
GTT.  Copying 32 MiB buffers into and out of the peer's VRAM, in full and
at random sub-ranges, the CPU checked 15 GiB over five runs through host
staging with no mismatches, and words outside each sub-range were left
intact.  Peer writes ran at 7.9 GB/s and peer reads at 3.7 GB/s.
---

Notes:
    Testing beyond the commit message: xgpu p2p-verify (the test described
    above) also passed 3 of 3 runs on 7.2.9 and on 7.3-rc7 kernels carrying
    this entry, on Mac Pro 6,1s.  I have not compared the same kernel and
    config with and without only this entry; without it,
    pci_p2pdma_distance() refuses the pair and amdgpu falls back to
    migrating the import to GTT.  0e01 (the DMI2 port in PCIe mode, the
    analogue of 3c01) is left out because I have no system that presents it.
    
    How this was made: an AI coding assistant (Claude, in Claude Code) wrote
    the patch and this message at my direction and ran the tests on my
    machines.

 drivers/pci/p2pdma.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/p2pdma.c b/drivers/pci/p2pdma.c
index 45260423dfb0..fd109c63e0e3 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/p2pdma.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/p2pdma.c
@@ -543,6 +543,8 @@ static const struct pci_p2pdma_whitelist_entry {
 	/* Intel Xeon E5/Core i7 */
 	{PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL,	0x3c00, REQ_SAME_HOST_BRIDGE},
 	{PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL,	0x3c01, REQ_SAME_HOST_BRIDGE},
+	/* Intel Xeon E7 v2/Xeon E5 v2/Core i7 */
+	{PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL,	0x0e00, REQ_SAME_HOST_BRIDGE},
 	/* Intel Xeon E7 v4/Xeon E5 v4/Xeon E3 v4/Xeon D */
 	{PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL,	0x6f00, REQ_SAME_HOST_BRIDGE},
 	/* Intel Xeon E7 v3/Xeon E5 v3/Core i7 */

